<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1001B_S000A" variety="S000A">
<name>Wiper &amp; Washer</name>
<ttl id="1001B_S000A_7421P_T001Z" variety="T001Z">
<name>Washer Nozzle</name>
<para id="RM000001XEJ003X" category="N" type-id="3000G" name-id="611DL-00" from="200612">
<name>Adjustment</name>
<subpara id="RM000001XEJ003X_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM000001XEJ003X_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000V700000">
<ptxt>Adjust Washer Nozzle</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a screwdriver with its tip wrapped in protective tape, disengage the 2 claws in the order indicated by the arrows in the illustration, and separate the washer nozzle.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E145490J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not damage the glass.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the washer nozzle from the washer hose.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E125282" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The washer nozzle cannot be reused.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Select and replace the washer nozzle so that the washer fluid spray lands within the standard range.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E139091J01" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
